## 2. Grant of Permissions

Subject to the terms of this license, You are granted a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to:

### 2.1 Personal & Educational Use
(a) Use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, and sublicense the Software for personal projects, educational purposes, academic research, and open-source projects;

(b) Create and share Derivative Works for non-commercial purposes;

(c) Use the Software in tutorials, courses, books, and educational content.

### 2.2 Internal Commercial Use
(a) Use the Software internally within Your organization for development, testing, evaluation, and internal tooling;

(b) Build internal tools, prototypes, and proof-of-concepts using the Software;

(c) Evaluate the Software for potential adoption in commercial products.

### 2.3 Commercial Product Development
(a) Build and sell products or services that incorporate or are built with the Software, subject to Section 3;

(b) Create Derivative Works for commercial distribution, subject to Section 3;

(c) Use the Software in client projects, freelance work, and consulting engagements, subject to Section 3.

---

## 3. Commercial Use Conditions

If You engage in Commercial Use of the Software, You must comply with the following conditions:

### 3.1 Attribution Requirement
Include the following attribution in all user-facing documentation, about pages, credits, or product descriptions:

> "Built with Maxilun — https://github.com/giriedu/maxilun"

For digital products, this attribution must be visible in the application's settings, about page, or footer. For physical products or services, include the attribution in accompanying documentation.

### 3.2 License Retention
Retain this license text and copyright notice in all copies or substantial portions of the Software, including Derivative Works.

### 3.3 Notice of Commercial Use
Provide written notice to Maxilun Architecture at **license@maxilun.com** describing the nature of Your commercial use within 30 days of first commercial deployment. This notice helps us understand how Maxilun is being used and supports community-driven improvements.

### 3.4 Revenue Threshold Exemption
Organizations with annual revenue below USD $1,000,000 (or equivalent in local currency) are exempt from the notification requirement in Section 3.3, but must still comply with Sections 3.1 and 3.2.

---

## 4. Restrictions

You may NOT:

### 4.1 Managed Service Restriction
Sell, resell, rent, lease, or offer the Software itself as a Managed Service without prior written permission from Maxilun Architecture. This includes:
- Hosting Maxilun as a service where users interact with Maxilun's core functionality
- Offering "Maxilun-as-a-Service" or similar branded offerings
- Providing API access to Maxilun's skill execution engine as a standalone service

**Exception**: Using Maxilun to build and host Your own distinct product or service is permitted under Section 2.3.

### 4.2 Proprietary Notices
Remove, alter, or obscure any copyright, patent, trademark, or proprietary notices contained in the Software.

### 4.3 Legal Compliance
Use the Software in violation of applicable laws or regulations, including export control laws, data protection regulations, and intellectual property laws.

### 4.4 False Endorsement
Represent that You are endorsed by or affiliated with Maxilun Architecture beyond what this license permits. Do not use Maxilun trademarks, logos, or branding in a way that suggests official partnership or endorsement without written permission.

### 4.5 Competitive Forking
Distribute a fork of the Software that competes directly with Maxilun's core offering without significant differentiation in features, target audience, or value proposition. Community forks for experimentation, education, or niche use cases are permitted.

